`expanded`, `readWrite`, `readOnly`\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:60:- **`startShapes`**: a five-key count in `tallyBlock`, filled only where `started` is counted\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:78:| `tallyBlock`, the text summary | Print the start rate | Add `startShapes` | Rescore check |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:85:- Algorithm invariant: `startShapes` sums to `started` in every block, and `startRate` does not change.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:51:- `startShapes` per runtime and arm in the scorer summary\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:61:`lib/metrics.ts` keeps durable health records under `join(tmpdir(), 'speckit-skill-advisor-metrics')`, and the suite runs with the operator's own temp folder, so every suite run adds test records to the folder that the health readers and the research lanes read as real use. Separately, the scorer's printed start rate counts a document read with no write as a start, while the goal's fixed arm start rule calls that a lookup, and no printed number says how many starts are of that kind.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:80:claude off startRate 2 of 15 startShapes absent\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:79:| `scorer/fusion.ts` `readOnlyRouteAllowed`, `commandMeaningEligible` | Second reader of the no-edit wording | update