tatement, When the goal log and README are read, Then two `Start rates, fixed rule` rows exist and the README states the rule and `startShapes` | `rg -c` prints 2 for `Start rates, fixed rule` rows in `../goal.md`, plus the pre and final set rows. README `rg -c startShapes` prints 2 | Met | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n| `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n| `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n\n### Waiver cell\n\nWrite `-` when the row is `Met` or `Unmet`. Write `ADR-NNN` when the row is\n`Waived` or `Superseded`, naming a decision record that exists in\n`decision-record.md`. A waiver naming an ADR that is not there fails validation:\nthe point of a waiver is that someone recorded the reasoning, so an unbacked\nwaiver is treated as an unmet criterion rather than as a pass.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:closure -->\n## 3. CLOSURE STATEMENT\n<!-- FILL: Write Yes or No and one sentence. Name a criterion by its id only when it blocks closure. Never write a count of criteria or an id range, because every added row makes it wrong. GOOD: No. AC-002 is unmet. WEAK: All eight criteria AC-001 to AC-008 are met. -->\n\n**Closeable:** Yes\n\nEvery row is Met with the evidence it names.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:closure -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/036-start-rate-fixed-rule/acceptance-criteria.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816107890,"end":1794816108399}}}}
