{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816209092,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e361eb0e001k7HW0h6h6zccAj","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","messageID":"msg_1e3616ac2001nvZCD770qntQig","type":"tool","id":"call_87d9e1973e0a4259b3f34521","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && node -e \"\nconst fs=require('fs');\nconst r=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/deep-review-findings-registry.json','utf8'));\nconst seen=new Set();\nfor(const f of [...(r.openFindings||[]),...(r.resolvedFindings||[])]){\n  const t=f.title||'';\n  if(seen.has(t)) continue; seen.add(t);\n  console.log(f.severity, '|', t, '|', (f.file||'').split('/').pop()+':'+f.line, '|', (f._lineages||[]).join(','));\n}\n\" | sort | head -80"},"output":"P1 | `make no changes to` reads a genuine no-edit request as a change request | command-attach.ts:289 | noedit-confirm-3b\nP1 | A coordinated refusal names the second command without a lead, so the typed path still delivers it | command-attach.ts:414 | scorer-attach-4\nP1 | A failed write mid-apply leaves a half-embedded tree and prints no undo | agents-md-embed.cjs:1364 | doctor-install\nP1 | A fully-permissioned measured turn inherits operator credentials and can reach hosts the repo-remote guard does not cover | run-command-behaviour.mjs:782 | accuracy-runner\nP1 | A symlinked REPO RULES.md or .cursor/rules/repo-local.md is written through, so apply mutates a file its plan never named | agents-md-embed.cjs:783 | doctor-install\nP1 | An attached node evaluation flag still reports the hook as wired | hook-wiring-check.cjs:266 | doctor-docs-3\nP1 | An or-list refusal that names its second command as \"the /x command\" still attaches that command | command-attach.ts:379 | scorer-attach-confirm-4b\nP1 | An or-list whose non-final item is a two-word /doctor command still publishes the refused command | command-attach.ts:380 | scorer-attach-close-4c\nP1 | Committed baseline publishes per-row holdout outcomes and a test pins them | capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:537 | accuracy-runner\nP1 | In-place shell edits are never write events, so unsafe and loopInit miss every write that is not a redirect | score-command-transcripts.mjs:391 | accuracy-runner-5\nP1 | NO_EDIT_REQUEST omits the write verbs, so dont create it yet keeps a mutating command | command-attach.ts:292 | noedit-close-3c\nP1 | The arena's build output comes from the working tree while its tracked tree comes from HEAD, and no step checks that the two agree | prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:310 | accuracy-runner-5\nP1 | The child-session command downgrade is decided only by a process-wide env flag | render.ts:522 | render-hooks-plugin\nP1 | The containment guard runs before the first turn only, so a git remote added by any turn survives the restore and a later turn can push | run-command-behaviour.mjs:1264 | accuracy-runner-5\nP1 | The contracted \"make changes\" instruction is not in the no-edit vocabulary, so a mutating command is offered on a plain no-edit prompt | command-attach.ts:292 | hook-close-3c\nP1 | The make-no-changes lookahead is over-broad: a genuine no-edit request that names its object loses the guard | command-attach.ts:289 | hook-confirm-3b\nP1 | The partner-side offer field is computed and then dropped by both offer writers | command-offer.mjs:486 | accuracy-runner-4\nP1 | The refusal and question rows can still carry a command, and no gate consumes the count | capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:595 | accuracy-runner-4\nP2 | --backfill executes the hook and the advisor CLI from the directory a run-log line names | command-offer.mjs:333 | accuracy-runner-2\nP2 | --backfill replays a started-command row with the default fixture path even when the run used a custom --fixture | run-command-behaviour.mjs:1214 | accuracy-runner-2\nP2 | `make no changes` reads a scope-limiting change request as a no-edit request | command-attach.ts:289 | advisor-runtime-3\nP2 | A --target-directory copy records the source as the file it changed | score-command-transcripts.mjs:1040 | accuracy-runner-confirm-5b\nP2 | A 2> or &> redirect target that names a command document still counts as a start | score-command-transcripts.mjs:677 | accuracy-runner-close-4c\nP2 | A background & is folded into the writer's argument list | score-command-transcripts.mjs:895 | accuracy-runner-confirm-5b\nP2 | A command that starts after a shell keyword or the command builtin is not read as a command start | hook-wiring-check.cjs:240 | hook-close-3c\nP2 | A correction inside one document still attaches the creation workflow when the sentence carries a generic creation word | command-attach.ts:487 | scorer-attach-4\nP2 | A corrupt Devin sessions.db suppresses the transcript fallback | devin.mjs:395 | render-hooks-plugin\nP2 | A documented timeout consumer never reads the timeout variable | skill-advisor-hook.md:176 | render-hooks-plugin\nP2 | A dotenv file tracked in the commit under test is cloned into the arena, because the dotenv guard runs only on the copied build trees | prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:275 | accuracy-runner-5\nP2 | A DSH operator message with no source object is silently reclassified as injected | dsh.mjs:195 | render-hooks-plugin\nP2 | A file name git quotes cannot be restored, so one space in a created path stops the arm and leaves the file | worktree-restore.mjs:54 | accuracy-runner-2\nP2 | A fourth hand-spelled runtime list sits outside the parity test that exists to catch exactly this | index.mjs:28 | render-hooks-plugin\nP2 | A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands | score-command-transcripts.mjs:647 | accuracy-runner-4\nP2 | A long flag whose value is attached by shell quoting still reports ok for a command node refuses to run | hook-wiring-check.cjs:232 | noedit-confirm-3b\nP2 |