`sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A run line stored before the writers kept `offeredAs` holds none, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. `startRate` counts a row as started on the same rule the decline and skill-only counts use, set out next, so a read of the command's document with no write in the checkout is a lookup and not a start. `startShapes` splits the uncapped rows that started or looked up into `skill`, `reported`, `expanded`, `readWrite` and `readOnly`, judged in that order so a run counts once under its strongest evidence. The first four sum to the started count and `readOnly` counts the lookups, and the text output prints them as a `start shapes` segment. `startedOfOffered` and each `byPolicy` `started` count follow the same rule, and `readOnly` restores only the `startRate` numerator. A decline or skill-only run started a tracked command when a skill call named it, a `COMMAND:` line reported it `started`, the host expanded it, or the run read the command's document and also wrote inside its checkout. A read with no write is a lookup and not a start, and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line is not a read, so `declineStarts` and `skillOnlyStarts` print as `x of y` over those runs and `commandStartRuns` lists each start with its row, run, command and offered command. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n115:Each arm's `startRate`, `startedOfOffered` and each policy's `started` count in `byPolicy` follow the start rule bel\n135:| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"A start and a loop the run took\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md; grep -n \\\"startRate.*counts a row as started\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md; grep -n \\\"startShapes\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | cut -c1-120\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816339712,"end":1794816340852}}}}
