{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816487989,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e365f605001NnTtwh2HA6uALS","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","messageID":"msg_1e365e2e70014w0df8NGAF6wDM","type":"tool","id":"call_2314c73758b74c43be929d1c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the pass-six `scorer-6` review lineage. The lineage reviews the transcript scorer, its vitest file and the routing-accuracy README only: the heredoc redirect fix, the start shape split and the rule that a document read with no checkout write is a lookup. Every finding is P0/P1/P2 with file:line and a concrete input.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Init wrote the topic, dimensions, known context and boundaries below.\n- Each iteration reads Next Focus, reviews one dimension, updates the running counts and sets the next focus.\n- Mutability: mutable, updated by each iteration. Machine-owned blocks are between explicit markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nPass-six code review of the command-surfacing transcript scorer: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`. Net diff `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff ddb12a6852c 85550ee946e` covers phase 034 (heredoc redirect fix), the empty-heredoc end-line fix, phase 035 (start shapes) and phase 036 (a read alone is a lookup). Review target is the spec folder `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] D1 Correctness\n- [ ] D2 Security\n- [ ] D3 Traceability\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The `arena-config` and `merge-docs` areas other lineages own in pass six.\n- The runner, advisor, arena builder, row files and run logs; only the scorer and its own docs are in scope.\n- Any code change. The lineage reports findings only.\n- Holdout prompt text: never read, printed or quoted, at any point.\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits unless a new input breaks them.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1 or `maxIterations` 3, whichever comes first.\n- A P0 finding halts the PASS claim but not the iteration loop.\n- Any write outside `review/lineages/scorer-6/` stops the lineage.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [ ] correctness\n- [ ] security\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the packet's phase 034/035/036 specs before choosing a focus.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- None yet.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n- None yet.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- None yet.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: correctness - Focus area: `redirectTargets`/`HEREDOC_BODY` heredoc stripping and the `startShape` read-alone rule - Reason: the net diff's two behavioural changes - Rotation status: open - Required evidence: a probe or read that shows the input's effect on a write event or on `started` - Recovery note: none\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (about 2700 lines; exports `normalize`, `startState`, `startedCommand`, `insideCheckout`, `commandLines`, `loopInit` for direct tests), `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` (about 3500 lines), `routing-accuracy/README.md` (scorer row at line 135, start rule at line 115).\n- Behaviour claims to verify: `redirectTargets` strips heredoc bodies before it scans for `>`; an empty heredoc body ends at its own end line and a backslash-quoted end word is honoured; `startState` returns a shape and counts a read alone as `readOnly`; `startShapes` sums to `started` over uncapped start rows; `startRate`, `startedOfOffered` and `byPolicy.started` all read the same `started` fact.\n- Reuse and conventions: `firstWritePosition(events, checkoutDir)` is the single write-boundary helper; `insideCheckout` treats a relative path as inside and a `/tmp`, `/var/folders` or `~` path as outside; `writePaths` keeps a write whose target the record never names as `[null]`; `documentTails` matches a command document by path tail.\n- Review risks and gaps: the packet registry holds 164 prior findings, so deduplication against `deep-review-findings-registry.json` is mandatory; the brief forbids `--summary`, so numeric rescore claims cannot be re-verified; holdout prompt text must never be read or printed.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | - | - | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | pending |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | - | - | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | pending |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | - | - | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | pending |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: 3\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-16T08:07:33Z\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for the pass-six `scorer-6` review lineage. The lineage reviews the transcript scorer, its vitest file and the routing-accuracy README only: the heredoc redirect fix, the start shape split and the rule that a document read with no checkout write is a lookup. Every finding is P0/P1/P2 with file:line and a concrete input.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- Init wrote the topic, dimensions, known context and boundaries below.\\n- Each iteration reads Next Focus, reviews one dimension, updates the running counts and sets the next focus.\\n- Mutability: mutable, updated by each iteration. Machine-owned blocks are between explicit markers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nPass-six code review of the command-surfacing transcript scorer: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`. Net diff `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff ddb12a6852c 85550ee946e` covers phase 034 (heredoc redirect fix), the empty-heredoc end-line fix, phase 035 (start shapes) and phase 036 (a read alone is a lookup). Review target is the spec folder `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness\\n- [ ] D2 Security\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- The `arena-config` and `merge-docs` areas other lineages own in pass six.\\n- The runner, advisor, arena builder, row files and run logs; only the scorer and its own docs are in scope.\\n- Any code change. The lineage reports findings only.\\n- Holdout prompt text: never read, printed or quoted, at any point.\\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits unless a new input breaks them.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1 or `maxIterations` 3, whichever comes first.\\n- A P0 finding halts the PASS claim but not the iteration loop.\\n- Any write outside `review/lineages/scorer-6/` stops the lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n- [ ] correctness\\n- [ ] security\\n- [ ] traceability\\n- [ ] maintainability\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\\n- P1 (Required): 0\\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\\n- Resolved: 0\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the packet's phase 034/035/036 specs before choosing a focus.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- None yet.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n- None yet.\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n- None yet.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n- Dimension: correctness - Focus area: `redirectTargets`/`HEREDOC_BODY` heredoc stripping and the `startShape` read-alone rule - Reason: the net diff's two behavioural changes - Rotation status: open - Required evidence: a probe or read that shows the input's effect on a write event or on `started` - Recovery note: none\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (about 2700 lines; exports `normalize`, `startState`, `startedCommand`, `insideCheckout`, `commandLines`, `loopInit` for direct tests), `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` (about 3500 lines), `routing-accuracy/README.md` (scorer row at line 135, start rule at line 115).\\n- Behaviour claims to verify: `redirectTargets` strips heredoc bodies before it scans for `>`; an empty heredoc body ends at its own end line and a backslash-quoted end word is honoured; `startState` returns a shape and counts a read alone as `readOnly`; `startShapes` sums to `started` over uncapped start rows; `startRate`, `startedOfOffered` and `byPolicy.started` all read the same `started` fact.\\n- Reuse and conventions: `firstWritePosition(events, checkoutDir)` is the single write-boundary helper; `insideCheckout` treats a relative path as inside and a `/tmp`, `/var/folders` or `~` path as outside; `writePaths` keeps a write whose target the record never names as `[null]`; `documentTails` matches a command document by path tail.\\n- Review risks and gaps: the packet registry holds 164 prior findings, so deduplication against `deep-review-findings-registry.json` is mandatory; the brief forbids `--summary`, so numeric rescore claims cannot be re-verified; holdout prompt text must never be read or printed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | - | - | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | pending |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | - | - | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | pending |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system