{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816588211,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e3678148001qdCvlzZHnUOdtf","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","messageID":"msg_1e3676d5e001Z4m7tdkGFWvT06","type":"tool","id":"call_58fd39de25fc4d97b20079b9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && node -e \"\nconst fs=require('fs');\nconst dir='specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6';\nconst record={\n type:'iteration',iteration:1,mode:'review',target_agent:'deep-review',agent_definition_loaded:true,\n resolved_route:'Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review',\n run:'fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p',status:'complete',\n focus:'correctness -- heredoc redirect stripping and the read-alone start rule',\n dimensions:['correctness'],\n filesReviewed:[\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:255-300',\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:315-328',\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:711-760',\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1370-1520',\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2140-2260',\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2380-2420',\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:250-300',\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1469-1530',\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:2165-2195',\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:112-135'\n ],\n findingsCount:2,\n findingsSummary:{P0:0,P1:0,P2:2},\n findingsNew:['iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write','iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout'],\n findingDetails:[\n  {\n   id:'iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write',severity:'P2',title:'A second heredoc on one opening line is not stripped, so its body comparison becomes a write',\n   dimension:'correctness',file:'.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:752',\n   claim:'HEREDOC_BODY keeps the rest of the opening line after the first delimiter in group 1, so a line that lists two heredocs consumes only the first body and leaves the second body in the scanned text, where a comparison reads as a redirect.',\n   evidenceRefs:['.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:752','.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:269'],\n   counterevidenceSought:'Ran the two-delimiter command through normalize, then re-read the pattern to confirm the second delimiter lands in group 1 rather than in a body. Checked the packet registry for an existing finding with this input; the recorded heredoc finding names a delimiter that is not a bare identifier, a different input.',\n   alternativeExplanation:'A shell that lists two heredocs on one line is uncommon and the pre-fix pattern behaved the same way, so the gap may be accepted as out of reach; that reading leaves the fix comment (a heredoc body is data) untrue for an input the pattern claims to strip, and the false write moves the first-write boundary.',\n   finalSeverity:'P2',confidence:0.9,\n   downgradeTrigger:'Downgrade to ruled-out if the corpus and runner never emit a shell command with more than one heredoc delimiter on one line.',\n   findingClass:'correctness',\n   scopeProof:'The pattern, its redirect consumer and the shell write scanner are all inside the pass-six scoped scorer file.',\n   affectedSurfaceHints:['HEREDOC_BODY','redirectTargets','shellWriteTargets','firstWritePosition','workflowPath','startShape']\n  },\n  {\n   id:'iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout',severity:'P2',title:'A write whose target is never named counts as inside the checkout, so a lookup plus an unnamed write scores as a readWrite start',\n   dimension:'correctness',file:'.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:327',\n   claim:'writePaths keeps a write with no target as [null], and firstWritePosition skips a write only when its path is a string outside the checkout, so an unnamed write satisfies the inside-checkout test that startShape uses for readWrite.',\n   evidenceRefs:['.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:327','.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:729','.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1513'],\n   counterevidenceSought:'Probed a Read of the command document plus a Write tool call with no path key, and a Read plus a Bash apply_patch whose body used ---/+++ headers; both produced one unnamed write and startState returned readWrite with started true. Checked whether any later step removes the unnamed write before the boundary; none does.',\n   alternativeExplanation:'A write with no named target is still a write, so counting it may be the conservative choice; that choice is conservative for unsafe but not for the start rule, where phase 036 defines the start as a write inside the checkout and an unknown folder is not evidence of one.',\n   finalSeverity:'P2',confidence:0.85,\n   downgradeTrigger:'Downgrade to ruled-out if every scoped runtime always records a target for a write tool call and for apply_patch.',\n   findingClass:'correctness',\n   scopeProof:'writePaths, firstWritePosition and startShape are the scoped scorer own boundary path, and the phase 036 edge-case row names the outside-checkout write as a lookup.',\n   affectedSurfaceHints:['writePaths','firstWritePosition','insideCheckout','startShape','startRate','startShapes.readWrite']\n  }\n ],\n traceabilityChecks:{results:[\n  {protocolId:'spec_code',status:'pass',gateClass:'hard',applicable:true,evidence:['.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1494-1518','.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1504'],summary:'Phase 036 REQ-004 maps to the startState shape return and its cases; REQ-001 follows by construction, and its numeric restatement is not re-run because the brief forbids --summary.'}\n ]},\n newFindingsRatio:1.0,\n noveltyJustification:'First iteration of the lineage: two findings, neither present in the packet registry by title or by input, weighted new 2 of weighted total 2.',\n sessionId:'fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p',generation:1,lineageMode:'new',\n timestamp:'2026-11-16T08:09:27Z',durationMs:59000,\n graphEvents:[\n  {type:'node',id:'file-scorer',kind:'FILE',label:'score-command-transcripts.mjs'},\n  {type:'node',id:'bug-second-heredoc-body',kind:'BUG_CLASS',label:'second heredoc body left in the redirect scan'},\n  {type:'node',id:'bug-unnamed-write-boundary',kind:'BUG_CLASS',label:'unnamed write counted as inside the checkout'},\n  {type:'edge',id:'edge-1',source:'bug-second-heredoc-body',target:'file-scorer',relation:'IN_FILE'},\n  {type:'edge',id:'edge-2',source:'bug-unnamed-write-boundary',target:'file-scorer',relation:'IN_FILE'}\n ]\n};\nfs.writeFileSync(dir+'/iter-001.record.json',JSON.stringify(record)+'\\n');\nconsole.log('record bytes',JSON.stringify(record).length);\n\""},"output":"record bytes 7020\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"record bytes 7020\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && node -e \\\"\\nconst fs=require('fs');\\nconst dir='specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6';\\nconst record={\\n type:'iteration',iteration:1,mode:'review',target_agent:'deep-review',agent_definition_loaded:true,\\n resolved_route:'Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review',\\n run:'fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p',status:'complete',\\n focus:'correctness -- heredoc redirect stripping and the read-alone start rule',\\n dimensions:['correctness'],\\n filesReviewed:[\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:255-300',\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:315-328',\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:711-760',\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1370-1520',\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2140-2260',\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2380-2420',\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:250-300',\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1469-1530',\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:2165-2195',\\n  '.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:112-135'\\n ],\\n findingsCount:2,\\n findingsSummary:{P0:0,P1:0,P2:2},\\n findingsNew:['iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write','iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout'],\\n findingDetails:[\\n  {\\n   id:'iter1-P2-second-heredoc-body-write',severity:'P2',title:'A second heredoc on one opening line is not stripped, so its body comparison becomes a write',\\n   dimension:'correctness',file:'.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:752',\\n   claim:'HEREDOC_BODY keeps the rest of the opening line after the first delimiter in group 1, so a line that lists two heredocs consumes only the first body and leaves the second body in the scanned text, where a comparison reads as a redirect.',\\n   evidenceRefs:['.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:752','.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:269'],\\n   counterevidenceSought:'Ran the two-delimiter command through normalize, then re-read the pattern to confirm the second delimiter lands in group 1 rather than in a body. Checked the packet registry for an existing finding with this input; the recorded heredoc finding names a delimiter that is not a bare identifier, a different input.',\\n   alternativeExplanation:'A shell that lists two heredocs on one line is uncommon and the pre-fix pattern behaved the same way, so the gap may be accepted as out of reach; that reading leaves the fix comment (a heredoc body is data) untrue for an input the pattern claims to strip, and the false write moves the first-write boundary.',\\n   finalSeverity:'P2',confidence:0.9,\\n   downgradeTrigger:'Downgrade to ruled-out if the corpus and runner never emit a shell command with more than one heredoc delimiter on one line.',\\n   findingClass:'correctness',\\n   scopeProof:'The pattern, its redirect consumer and the shell write scanner are all inside the pass-six scoped scorer file.',\\n   affectedSurfaceHints:['HEREDOC_BODY','redirectTargets','shellWriteTargets','firstWritePosition','workflowPath','startShape']\\n  },\\n  {\\n   id:'iter1-P2-unnamed-write-is-inside-checkout',severity:'P2',title:'A write whose target is never named counts as inside the checkout, so a lookup plus an unnamed write scores as a readWrite start',\\n   dimension:'correctness',file:'.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:327',\\n   claim:'writePaths keeps a write with no target as [null], and firstWritePosition skips a write only when its path is a string outside the checkout, so an unnamed write satisfies the inside-checkout test that startShape uses for readWrite.',\\n   evidenceRefs:['.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:327','.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:729','.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1513'],\\n   counterevidenceSought:'Probed a Read of the command document plus a Write tool call with no path key, and a Read plus a Bash apply_patch whose body used ---/+++ headers; both produced one unnamed write and startState returned readWrite with started true. Checked whether any later step removes the unnamed write before the boundary; none does.',\\n   alternativeExplanation:'A write with no named target is still a write, so counting it may be the conservative choice; that choice is conservative for unsafe but not for the start rule, where phase 036 defines the start as a write inside the checkout and an unknown folder is not evidence of one.',\\n   finalSeverity:'P2',confidence:0.85,\\n   downgradeTrigger:'Downgrade to ruled-out if every scoped runtime always records a target for a write tool call and for apply_patch.',\\n   findingClass:'correctness',\\n   scopeProof:'writePaths, firstWritePosition and startShape are the scoped scorer own boundary path, and the phase 036 edge-case row names the outside-checkout write as a lookup.',\\n   affectedSurfaceHints:['writePaths','firstWritePosition','insideCheckout','startShape','startRate','startShapes.readWrite']\\n  }\\n ],\\n traceabilityChecks:{results:[\\n  {protocolId:'spec_code',status:'pass',gateClass:'hard',applicable:true,evidence:['.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1494-1518','.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1504'],summary:'Phase 036 REQ-004 maps to the startState shape return and its cases; REQ-001 follows by construction, and its numeric restatement is not re-run because the brief forbids --summary.'}\\n ]},\\n newFindingsRatio:1.0,\\n noveltyJustification:'First iteration of the lineage: two findings, neither present in the packet registry by title or by input, weighted new 2 of weighted total 2.',\\n sessionId:'fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p',generation:1,lineageMode:'new',\\n timestamp:'2026-11-16T08:09:27Z',durationMs:59000,\\n graphEvents:[\\n  {type:'node',id:'file-scorer',kind:'FILE',label:'score-command-transcripts.mjs'},\\n  {type:'node',id:'bug-second-heredoc-body',kind:'BUG_CLASS',label:'second heredoc body left in the redirect scan'},\\n  {type:'node',id:'bug-unnamed-write-boundary',kind:'BUG_CLASS',label:'unnamed write counted as inside the checkout'},\\n  {type:'edge',id:'edge-1',source:'bug-second-heredoc-body',target:'file-scorer',relation:'IN_FILE'},\\n  {type:'edge',id:'edge-2',source:'bug-unnamed-write-boundary',target:'file-scorer',relation:'IN_FILE'}\\n ]\\n};\\nfs.writeFileSync(dir+'/iter-001.record.json',JSON.stringify(record)+'\\\\n');\\nconsole.log('record bytes',JSON.stringify(record).length);\\n\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816573768,"end":1794816588211}}}}
