mmand-surfacing-build`.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n24: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n25: - [ ] security\n26: - [ ] traceability\n27: - [ ] maintainability\n28: \n29: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n30: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n31: \n32: - The `arena-config` and `merge-docs` areas other lineages own in pass six.\n33: - The runner, advisor, arena builder, row files and run logs; only the scorer and its own docs are in scope.\n34: - Any code change. The lineage reports findings only.\n35: - Holdout prompt text: never read, printed or quoted, at any point.\n36: - Re-reporting the recorded limits unless a new input breaks them.\n37: \n38: ---\n39: \n40: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n41: \n42: - Convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1 or `maxIterations` 3, whichever comes first.\n43: - A P0 finding halts the PASS claim but not the iteration loop.\n44: - Any write outside `review/lineages/scorer-6/` stops the lineage.\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n49: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n50: - [x] correctness\n51: \n52: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n53: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n54: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n55: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n56: - P1 (Required): 0\n57: - P2 (Suggestions): 2\n58: - Resolved: 0\n59: \n60: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n61: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n62: \n63: - Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the packet's phase 034/035/036 specs before choosing a focus.\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n68: \n69: - None yet.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n74: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n75: ### `readDocument` counting a `cat` of the document with a redirect as a shell read: normalize emits a write event instead of a shell event for a redirecting command, which the registry already records as \"A shell read counts as a workflow load but not as a start or a loop\". -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n76: - What was tried: `readDocument` counting a `cat` of the document with a redirect as a shell read: normalize emits a write event instead of a shell event for a redirecting command, which the registry already records as \"A shell read counts as a workflow load but not as a start or a loop\".\n77: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n78: - Do NOT retry: `readDocument` counting a `cat` of the document with a redirect as a shell read: normalize emits a write event instead of a shell event for a redirecting command, which the registry already records as \"A shell read counts as a workflow load but not as a start or a loop\".\n79: \n80: ### `startShape`'s skill/reported/expanded precedence changing a count: all four starting shapes add to `started`, so the order changes only which label a start carries. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n81: - What was tried: `startShape`'s skill/reported/expanded precedence changing a count: all four starting shapes add to `started`, so the order changes only which label a start carries.\n82: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n83: - Do NOT retry: `startShape`'s skill/reported/expanded precedence changing a count: all four starting shapes add to `started`, so the order changes only which label a start carries.\n84: \n85: ### A `$'EOF'` ANSI-C-quoted delimiter leaving its body in the scan: already recorded as an open P2 in the packet registry (\"A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands\"), so not re-reported; pass six fixed only the backslash form. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n86: - What was tried: A `$'EOF'` ANSI-C-quoted delimiter leaving its body in the scan: already recorded as an open P2 in the packet registry (\"A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands\"), so not re-reported; pass six fixed only the backslash form.\n87: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n88: - Do NOT retry