: - Target pointers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (about 2700 lines; exports `normalize`, `startState`, `startedCommand`, `insideCheckout`, `commandLines`, `loopInit` for direct tests), `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` (about 3500 lines), `routing-accuracy/README.md` (scorer row at line 135, start rule at line 115).\n120: - Behaviour claims to verify: `redirectTargets` strips heredoc bodies before it scans for `>`; an empty heredoc body ends at its own end line and a backslash-quoted end word is honoured; `startState` returns a shape and counts a read alone as `readOnly`; `startShapes` sums to `started` over uncapped start rows; `startRate`, `startedOfOffered` and `byPolicy.started` all read the same `started` fact.\n121: - Reuse and conventions: `firstWritePosition(events, checkoutDir)` is the single write-boundary helper; `insideCheckout` treats a relative path as inside and a `/tmp`, `/var/folders` or `~` path as outside; `writePaths` keeps a write whose target the record never names as `[null]`; `documentTails` matches a command document by path tail.\n122: - Review risks and gaps: the packet registry holds 164 prior findings, so deduplication against `deep-review-findings-registry.json` is mandatory; the brief forbids `--summary`, so numeric rescore claims cannot be re-verified; holdout prompt text must never be read or printed.\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n127: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n128: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n129: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n130: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n131: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n132: | `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n133: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n134: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n135: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n136: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n137: \n138: ---\n139: \n140: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n14