curacy README only: the heredoc redirect fix, the start shape split and the rule that a document read with no checkout write is a lookup. Every finding is P0/P1/P2 with file:line and a concrete input.\n8: \n9: ### Usage\n10: \n11: - Init wrote the topic, dimensions, known context and boundaries below.\n12: - Each iteration reads Next Focus, reviews one dimension, updates the running counts and sets the next focus.\n13: - Mutability: mutable, updated by each iteration. Machine-owned blocks are between explicit markers.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 2. TOPIC\n18: \n19: Pass-six code review of the command-surfacing transcript scorer: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`. Net diff `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff ddb12a6852c 85550ee946e` covers phase 034 (heredoc redirect fix), the empty-heredoc end-line fix, phase 035 (start shapes) and phase 036 (a read alone is a lookup). Review target is the spec folder `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n24: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n25: - [ ] security\n26: - [ ] traceability\n27: - [ ] maintainability\n28: \n29: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n30: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n31: \n32: - The `arena-config` and `merge-docs` areas other lineages own in pass six.\n33: - The runner, advisor, arena builder, row files and run logs; only the scorer and its own docs are in scope.\n34: - Any code change. The lineage reports findings only.\n35: - Holdout prompt text: never read, printed or quoted, at any point.\n36: - Re-reporting the recorded limits unless a new input breaks them.\n37: \n38: ---\n39: \n40: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n41: \n42: - Convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1 or `maxIterations` 3, whichever comes first.\n43: - A P0 finding halts the PASS claim but no