pts)\n81: - What was tried: `startShape`'s skill/reported/expanded precedence changing a count: all four starting shapes add to `started`, so the order changes only which label a start carries.\n82: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n83: - Do NOT retry: `startShape`'s skill/reported/expanded precedence changing a count: all four starting shapes add to `started`, so the order changes only which label a start carries.\n84: \n85: ### A `$'EOF'` ANSI-C-quoted delimiter leaving its body in the scan: already recorded as an open P2 in the packet registry (\"A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands\"), so not re-reported; pass six fixed only the backslash form. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n86: - What was tried: A `$'EOF'` ANSI-C-quoted delimiter leaving its body in the scan: already recorded as an open P2 in the packet registry (\"A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands\"), so not re-reported; pass six fixed only the backslash form.\n87: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n88: - Do NOT retry: A `$'EOF'` ANSI-C-quoted delimiter leaving its body in the scan: already recorded as an open P2 in the packet registry (\"A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands\"), so not re-reported; pass six fixed only the backslash form.\n89: \n90: ### A write outside the checkout defeating the read-alone rule when `projectDir` is present: the vitest case at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1520` pins it and the probe agrees. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n91: - What was tried: A write outside the checkout defeating the read-alone rule when `projectDir` is present: the vitest case at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1520` pins it and the probe agrees.\n92: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n93: - Do NOT retry: A write outside the checkout defeating the read-alone rule when `projectDir` is present: the vitest case at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1520` pins it and the probe agrees.\n94: \n95: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n96: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n97: - Completed pivots: 0\n98: - Failed pivots: 0\n99: - Audited overrides: 0\n100: - Swept: none yet\n101: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n102: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n103: \n104: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n105: \n106: - None yet.\n107: \n108: ---\n109: \n110: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n111: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n112: - Dimension: security and traceability (one cross-reference pass). - Focus area: holdout handling in `loadRowLabels`/`scoreRun`, and the README's start-rule sentences against the new code. - Reason: the correct path is read; the remaining risk is a doc that still states the old rule and any prompt leak in the label reader. - Rotation status: open. - Required evidence: a read of the label path and of every README sentence that names a start. Review verdict: PASS\n113: \n114: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n115: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n116: \n117: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n118: \n119: - Target pointers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (about 2700 lines; exports `normalize`, `startState`, `startedCommand`, `insideCheckout`, `commandLines`, `loopInit` for direct tests), `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` (about 3500 lines), `routing-accuracy/README.md` (scorer row at line 135, start rule at line 115).\n120: - Behaviour claims to verify: `redirectTargets` strips heredoc bodies before it scans for `>`; an empty heredoc body ends at its own end line and a backslash-quoted end word is honoured; `startState` returns a shape and counts a read alone as `readOnly`; `startShapes` sums to `started` over uncapped start rows; `startRate`, `startedOfOffered` and `byPolicy.started` all read the same `started` fact.\n121: - Reuse and conventions: `firstWritePosition(events, checkoutDir)` is the single write-boundary helper; `insideCheckout` treats a relative path as inside and a `/tmp`, `/var/folders` or `~` path as outside; `writePaths` keeps a write whose target the record never names as `[null]`; `documentTails` matches a command document by path tail.\n122: - Review risks and gaps: the packet registry holds 164 prior findings, so deduplication against `deep-review-findings-registry.json` is mandatory; the brief forbids `--summary`, so numeric rescore claims cannot be re-verified; holdout prompt text must never be read or printed.\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n127: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n128: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n129: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n130: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n131: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n132: | `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n133: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n134: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n135: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n136: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n137: \n138: ---\n139: \n140: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n141: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n142: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n143: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n144: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | - | - | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | pending |\n145: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | - | - | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | pending |\n146: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | - | - | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | pending |\n147: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n148: \n149: ---\n150: \n151: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n152: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n153: - Max iterations: 3\n154: - Convergence threshold: 0.1\n155: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n156: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n157: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n158: - Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-scorer-6-1794815529929-dybl7p, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n159: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n160: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n161: - Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n162: - Severity threshold: P2\n163: - Review target type: spec-folder\n164: - Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n165: - Started: 2026-11-16T08:07:33Z\n166: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816636711,"end":1794816636862}}}}
