{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816649668,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e3689e78002Ajyko6YOmyU5hE","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","messageID":"msg_1e3687bf6001n7xxVuoYEneJFd","type":"tool","id":"call_76b88512293c48f7927e3b33","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the packet's phase 034/035/036 specs before choosing a focus.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- None yet.","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the packet's phase 034/035/036 specs before choosing a focus.\n- Importing the scorer directly and running one `node --input-type=module -e` probe over crafted records turned both heredoc claims into observed event lists, without opening a prompt file or running `--summary` (iteration 1).\n- Reading `firstWritePosition` beside `writePaths` and `insideCheckout` isolated the unnamed-write boundary in one pass instead of a hunt through the tally (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Treating the new `HEREDOC_BODY` as a complete heredoc parser: its opening-line group still swallows a second delimiter, so a two-heredoc line leaves the second body scannable (iteration 1).\n- Assuming an unnamed write is dropped before the boundary: `writePaths` keeps it as `[null]` and `firstWritePosition` reads it as inside the checkout (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -60,14 +60,17 @@\n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n - Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the packet's phase 034/035/036 specs before choosing a focus.\n+- Importing the scorer directly and running one `node --input-type=module -e` probe over crafted records turned both heredoc claims into observed event lists, without opening a prompt file or running `--summary` (iteration 1).\n+- Reading `firstWritePosition` beside `writePaths` and `insideCheckout` isolated the unnamed-write boundary in one pass instead of a hunt through the tally (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-- None yet.\n+- Treating the new `HEREDOC_BODY` as a complete heredoc parser: its opening-line group still swallows a second delimiter, so a two-heredoc line leaves the second body scannable (iteration 1).\n+- Assuming an unnamed write is dropped before the boundary: `writePaths` keeps it as `[null]` and `firstWritePosition` reads it as inside the checkout (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the packet's phase 034/035/036 specs before choosing a focus.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- None yet.\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init read the brief, the scope file, the fan-out config and the packet's phase 034/035/036 specs before choosing a focus.\\n- Importing the scorer directly and running one `node --input-type=module -e` probe over crafted records turned both heredoc claims into observed event lists, without opening a prompt file or running `--summary` (iteration 1).\\n- Reading `firstWritePosition` beside `writePaths` and `insideCheckout` isolated the unnamed-write boundary in one pass instead of a hunt through the tally (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Treating the new `HEREDOC_BODY` as a complete heredoc parser: its opening-line group still swallows a second delimiter, so a two-heredoc line leaves the second body scannable (iteration 1).\\n- Assuming an unnamed write is dropped before the boundary: `writePaths` keeps it as `[null]` and `firstWritePosition` reads it as inside the checkout (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816646776,"end":1794816649668}}}}
