{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816736744,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e369bd720014hQreZ2B0stjaD","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","messageID":"msg_1e36984d2001UuDWKZHu4x71HV","type":"tool","id":"call_4f230ca3c11b4b64b030fb3e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `scorer-6`, area `scorer`, artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6`.\n- Review focus (pass six): the scorer area's holdout hygiene and the docs that describe the start rule, per `review-brief-6.txt`.\n- Dimension: security and traceability, run as one explicit cross-reference pass because the lineage has three iterations for four dimensions.\n- Sources read: the scoped scorer, the scoped vitest file, the scoped README, the packet's phase 035 and 036 acceptance criteria, and their `scratch/` evidence files. `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage directory.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1696-1717` (single-session mode), `:1723-1772` (label reader), `:2036-2056` (holdout refusal and unscored reasons), `:2590-2665` (every printed line).\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1560-1585` (shell-step start cases).\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:112-135`.\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/036-start-rate-fixed-rule/acceptance-criteria.md`, `scratch/restate.txt`, `scratch/restate-sets.txt`, `scratch/after.txt`.\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/scratch/shape-check.txt`.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The README and the shell-step test still say a bare document read is a start** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` -- the scorer row keeps the sentence \"A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts\", while the same row later states the new rule that a read with no write in the checkout is a lookup. The vitest comment above the shell-step table says the same thing (\"a reader that opens the document is the same start a read tool records\") even though every case in that table now also writes `src/parse.mjs`, so the `cat` case starts because of the write, not the read.\n   Finding class: traceability.\n   Scope proof: both files are pass-six scoped scorer files, and the disagreement is between the README's own two sentences in the same row.\n   Affected surface hints: `startRate`, `startShapes.readOnly`, `readDocument`, `startShape`, README scorer row, shell-step test comment.\n   Case: `cat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md` on a `/create:readme` row with no write — `startState` returns `{started: false, shape: 'readOnly'}` (probe, and the case at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1504`), so the README sentence and the test comment both describe a start that no longer happens.\n   Fix completeness: delete the `cat` clause from both sentences and leave the search, in-place `sed` and heredoc exclusions, which are still true.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code`: pass (carried). Phase 036 REQ-004 maps to `startState` and its cases; REQ-001's arithmetic holds by construction at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1494-1518`.\n- `checklist_evidence`: pass. `036-start-rate-fixed-rule/scratch/restate.txt` holds the 22 start lines reading `numerator moved by readOnly, denominator equal` plus the 10 decline lines reading `equal`; `restate-sets.txt` holds the 11 pre/final data lines plus two `other fields equal` rows; `after.txt` records `2326 passed` and the mutation check that the new summary lookup case fails when the shape tally moves back under `started`. The counts are the data lines the criteria name, so the evidence matches AC-001, AC-003 and AC-004.\n- Security/holdout: `loadRowLabels` keeps a holdout row as `{holdout: true}` only (`:1767`), `scoreRun` returns `holdout_row` before it reads a session (`:2050`), every printed line carries a row id, a reason code or a count (`:2593-2658`), and `scoreSession` prints a runtime, a session id and a record count (`:1714`). No prompt text reaches stdout.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH` is read only by the scorer (`:1732`) and set only by the scoped vitest file; no arm or scoring command sets it, so the holdout classification cannot be redirected by a tune or report path.\n- The packet's 036 checklist evidence is read as files, not re-scored: the brief forbids `--summary`, so no session store or corpus row was opened.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The AC-001 line count reads 22 while `restate.txt` holds 32 lines; the extra 10 are the decline lines, which the same file carries and AC-003 names. The 22 and the 11 are the data lines the criteria count, so this is a counting convention, not missing evidence.\n- `loadRowLabels` silently skips a missing fresh file, so fresh rows become `unknown_row` rather than a refusal. That path is unchanged by this branch and sits outside the diff's behaviour, so it is recorded here and not raised.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Holdout rows never reach a score, an output line or a reason; the refusal carries the reason code `holdout_row` only.\n- `--runtime --locator` loads a session and prints record counts; it never joins a row label and cannot print a prompt.\n- The README's new paragraph at line 115, its `startRate`/`startShapes` sentences in the row at line 135, and `byPolicy`/`startedOfOffered` all agree with `startState` and `addScored`.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A `SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH` redirect of a holdout row as a security hole: only the scoped test sets it, and a holdout row still needs a plain row with the same id in that file to be scored; recorded as ruled out rather than as a finding.\n- The scorer writing anything to disk: it has no filesystem write call; all of its writes are stdout.\n- A holdout row id in `unscoredRuns` as a leak: ids are committed in the corpus, and the reason carries no prompt.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability.\n- Focus area: the new `startShape` helper's contract against its callers and the `scoreRun` JSDoc, and the shape key list against `newTally`.\n- Reason: correctness, security and traceability are read; the remaining risk is documentation debt created by the same change.\n- Rotation status: open.\n- Required evidence: a read of every declaration the change touched and of the return-type block it did not.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `scorer-6`, area `scorer`, artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6`.\\n- Review focus (pass six): the scorer area's holdout hygiene and the docs that describe the start rule, per `review-brief-6.txt`.\\n- Dimension: security and traceability, run as one explicit cross-reference pass because the lineage has three iterations for four dimensions.\\n- Sources read: the scoped scorer, the scoped vitest file, the scoped README, the packet's phase 035 and 036 acceptance criteria, and their `scratch/` evidence files. `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage directory.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1696-1717` (single-session mode), `:1723-1772` (label reader), `:2036-2056` (holdout refusal and unscored reasons), `:2590-2665` (every printed line).\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1560-1585` (shell-step start cases).\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:112-135`.\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/036-start-rate-fixed-rule/acceptance-criteria.md`, `scratch/restate.txt`, `scratch/restate-sets.txt`, `scratch/after.txt`.\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/scratch/shape-check.txt`.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The README and the shell-step test still say a bare document read is a start** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` -- the scorer row keeps the sentence \\\"A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts\\\", while the same row later states the new rule that a read with no write in the checkout is a lookup. The vitest comment above the shell-step table says the same thing (\\\"a reader that opens the document is the same start a read tool records\\\") even though every case in that table now also writes `src/parse.mjs`, so the `cat` case starts because of the write, not the read.\\n   Finding class: traceability.\\n   Scope proof: both files are pass-six scoped scorer files, and the disagreement is between the README's own two sentences in the same row.\\n   Affected surface hints: `startRate`, `startShapes.readOnly`, `readDocument`, `startShape`, README scorer row, shell-step test comment.\\n   Case: `cat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md` on a `/create:readme` row with no write — `startState` returns `{started: false, shape: 'readOnly'}` (probe, and the case at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1504`), so the README sentence and the test comment both describe a start that no longer happens.\\n   Fix completeness: delete the `cat` clause from both sentences and leave the search, in-place `sed` and heredoc exclusions, which are still true.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code`: pass (carried). Phase 036 REQ-004 maps to `startState` and its cases; REQ-001's arithmetic holds by construction at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1494-1518`.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: pass. `036-start-rate-fixed-rule/scratch/restate.txt` holds the 22 start lines reading `numerator moved by readOnly, denominator equal` plus the 10 decline lines reading `equal`; `restate-sets.txt` holds the 11 pre/final data lines plus two `other fields equal` rows; `after.txt` records `2326 passed` and the mutation check that the new summary lookup case fails when the shape tally moves back under `started`. The counts are the data lines the criteria name, so the evidence matches AC-001, AC-003 and AC-004.\\n- Security/holdout: `loadRowLabels` keeps a holdout row as `{holdout: true}` only (`:1767`), `scoreRun` returns `holdout_row` before it reads a session (`:2050`), every printed line carries a row id, a reason code or a count (`:2593-2658`), and `scoreSession` prints a runtime, a session id and a record count (`:1714`). No prompt text reaches stdout.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH` is read only by the scorer (`:1732`) and set only by the scoped vitest file; no arm or scoring command sets it, so the holdout classification cannot be redirected by a tune or report path.\\n- The packet's 036 checklist evidence is read as files, not re-scored: the brief forbids `--summary`, so no session store or corpus row was opened.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The AC-001 line count reads 22 while `restate.txt` holds 32 lines; the extra 10 are the decline lines, which the same file carries and AC-003 names. The 22 and the 11 are the data lines the criteria count, so this is a counting convention, not missing evidence.\\n- `loadRowLabels` silently skips a missing fresh file, so fresh rows become `unknown_row` rather than a refusal. That path is unchanged by this branch and sits outside the diff's behaviour, so it is recorded here and not raised.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Holdout rows never reach a score, an output line or a reason; the refusal carries the reason code `holdout_row` only.\\n- `--runtime --locator` loads a session and prints record counts; it never joins a row label and cannot print a prompt.\\n- The README's new paragraph at line 115, its `startRate`/`startShapes` sentences in the row at line 135, and `byPolicy`/`startedOfOffered` all agree with `startState` and `addScored`.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A `SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH` redirect of a holdout row as a security hole: only the scoped test sets it, and a holdout row still needs a plain row with the same id in that file to be scored; recorded as ruled out rather than as a finding.\\n- The scorer writing anything to disk: it has no filesystem write call; all of its writes are stdout.\\n- A holdout row id in `unscoredRuns` as a leak: ids are committed in the corpus, and the reason carries no prompt.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability.\\n- Focus area: the new `startShape` helper's contract against its callers and the `scoreRun` JSDoc, and the shape key list against `newTally`.\\n- Reason: correctness, security and traceability are read; the remaining risk is documentation debt created by the same change.\\n- Rotation status: open.\\n- Required evidence: a read of every declaration the change touched and of the return-type block it did not.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816720242,"end":1794816736744}}}}
