{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816839921,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","part":{"partID":"prt_1e36b5aaf001fbupoN7Vqel8rz","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84ea7ffeYndeEpFMNWYowo","messageID":"msg_1e36b474f001TmAIm6thANxmz6","type":"tool","id":"call_8addf43685504cf4b62f9b3b","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `scorer-6`, area `scorer`, artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6`.\n- Review focus (pass six): the scorer area's maintainability and the final cross-reference pass for a scorer-only area.\n- Dimension: maintainability plus the overlay cross-reference resolutions.\n- Sources read: the scoped scorer's new helper and its consumer, the scoped vitest file, the scoped README, and the packet registry for deduplication. `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage directory.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1479-1520` (`startState` contract and `startShape`), `:2029-2042` (`scoreRun` return declaration), `:2083-2110` (the object `scoreRun` builds), `:2166-2190` (tally initialisation), `:2250-2262` (tally block), `:2400-2415` (`addScored`'s shape read), `:2590-2602` (text summary).\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1490-1530`, `:2165-2195`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:115`, `:135`.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **`scoreRun`'s declared return type omits `startShape`, the field `addScored` reads** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2035` -- the `@returns` union lists `startRow` and `started` but not `startShape`, which the same branch added at line 2104 and `addScored` reads at line 2412 with an `!== null` guard.\n   Finding class: maintainability.\n   Scope proof: the declaration and its only consumer are both in the pass-six scoped scorer file, and the field was added by this branch's diff.\n   Affected surface hints: `scoreRun` `@returns`, `addScored`, `startShapes`, `newTally`.\n   Case: a maintainer who edits `scoreRun` against its documented return type drops `startShape`; `addScored` then evaluates `undefined !== null` as true and writes `tally.startShapes[undefined] += 1`, so the summary prints an `undefined` key with a `NaN` (serialised as `null`) and the shape split stops summing to `started`.\n   Fix completeness: add `startShape: 'skill'|'reported'|'expanded'|'readWrite'|'readOnly'|null` to the `@returns` union, and key the tally from one exported shape list so the contract and the counters cannot drift.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code`: pass (carried). Phase 036 REQ-004 and REQ-001 map to `startState` and its cases as recorded in iteration 1.\n- `checklist_evidence`: pass (carried). The 036 `scratch/` files carry the counts AC-001, AC-003 and AC-004 name, and `after.txt` records the mutation check of the new summary case.\n- `skill_agent`: notApplicable. No skill file under `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor` names `score-command-transcripts`; only the folder README does.\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: notApplicable. No agent definition in `.skilled/agents/` or a runtime mirror names the scorer.\n- `feature_catalog_code`: notApplicable. The scorer is a measurement script, not a feature a catalog row describes.\n- `playbook_capability`: notApplicable. No playbook capability names the scorer.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The changed producer/consumer pair is `scoreRun` → `addScored`/`tallyBlock`/`writeSummary`, all inside the scoped file; no runtime mirror or command wrapper reads `startShape`.\n- The README row at line 135 and the paragraph at line 115 are the only documentation surfaces the change touches; both are in the scoped area.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `tally.startShapes[undefined] += 1` would not throw, which is why the missing field is a silent corruption rather than a crash: `undefined !== null` is true, and the increment creates an `undefined` key holding `NaN`.\n- A shape renamed in `startShape` alone would print a new key and leave the old key at zero; the same missing shared list is the root of both cases.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `startShape`'s comment states its order and its output vocabulary; `startState`'s JSDoc repeats the five names and the null case, so the public contract is documented even though the private consumer's declaration is not.\n- `tallyBlock` copies `startShapes` rather than sharing the tally object, so a printed block cannot mutate the tally.\n- The text summary prints all five shapes in a fixed insertion order, so a reader can compare two arms without parsing.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Raising the duplicated start rule (`startShape` versus `startedCommand`'s skill/report/expand/boundary sequence) as a finding: the two agree today, the comment in `readDocument` names both, and two instances do not justify a shared helper under the repository's restraint rule. Recorded as a follow-on risk, not a finding.\n- Raising the missing shared shape-key constant twice (in `newTally` and in `startShape`'s literals): folded into the finding above as its fix rather than counted again.\n- Calling the summary assertion `shapes.reduce(...) === 1` weak: its comment says it pins that the capped row adds no shape, and the same test's `startRate` assertion pins the started count, so it is fit for its stated purpose.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none; all four dimensions are covered and this is the third of three permitted iterations.\n- Focus area: synthesis.\n- Reason: `maxIterations` is reached; the remaining findings are three P2 advisories.\n- Rotation status: swept.\n- Required evidence: none outstanding.\n- Run verdict for this lineage: PASS with advisories (3 active P2, 0 P1, 0 P0).\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 003\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `scorer-6`, area `scorer`, artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6`.\\n- Review focus (pass six): the scorer area's maintainability and the final cross-reference pass for a scorer-only area.\\n- Dimension: maintainability plus the overlay cross-reference resolutions.\\n- Sources read: the scoped scorer's new helper and its consumer, the scoped vitest file, the scoped README, and the packet registry for deduplication. `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage directory.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1479-1520` (`startState` contract and `startShape`), `:2029-2042` (`scoreRun` return declaration), `:2083-2110` (the object `scoreRun` builds), `:2166-2190` (tally initialisation), `:2250-2262` (tally block), `:2400-2415` (`addScored`'s shape read), `:2590-2602` (text summary).\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1490-1530`, `:2165-2195`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:115`, `:135`.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **`scoreRun`'s declared return type omits `startShape`, the field `addScored` reads** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2035` -- the `@returns` union lists `startRow` and `started` but not `startShape`, which the same branch added at line 2104 and `addScored` reads at line 2412 with an `!== null` guard.\\n   Finding class: maintainability.\\n   Scope proof: the declaration and its only consumer are both in the pass-six scoped scorer file, and the field was added by this branch's diff.\\n   Affected surface hints: `scoreRun` `@returns`, `addScored`, `startShapes`, `newTally`.\\n   Case: a maintainer who edits `scoreRun` against its documented return type drops `startShape`; `addScored` then evaluates `undefined !== null` as true and writes `tally.startShapes[undefined] += 1`, so the summary prints an `undefined` key with a `NaN` (serialised as `null`) and the shape split stops summing to `started`.\\n   Fix completeness: add `startShape: 'skill'|'reported'|'expanded'|'readWrite'|'readOnly'|null` to the `@returns` union, and key the tally from one exported shape list so the contract and the counters cannot drift.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code`: pass (carried). Phase 036 REQ-004 and REQ-001 map to `startState` and its cases as recorded in iteration 1.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: pass (carried). The 036 `scratch/` files carry the counts AC-001, AC-003 and AC-004 name, and `after.txt` records the mutation check of the new summary case.\\n- `skill_agent`: notApplicable. No skill file under `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor` names `score-command-transcripts`; only the folder README does.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: notApplicable. No agent definition in `.skilled/agents/` or a runtime mirror names the scorer.\\n- `feature_catalog_code`: notApplicable. The scorer is a measurement script, not a feature a catalog row describes.\\n- `playbook_capability`: notApplicable. No playbook capability names the scorer.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The changed producer/consumer pair is `scoreRun` → `addScored`/`tallyBlock`/`writeSummary`, all inside the scoped file; no runtime mirror or command wrapper reads `startShape`.\\n- The README row at line 135 and the paragraph at line 115 are the only documentation surfaces the change touches; both are in the scoped area.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `tally.startShapes[undefined] += 1` would not throw, which is why the missing field is a silent corruption rather than a crash: `undefined !== null` is true, and the increment creates an `undefined` key holding `NaN`.\\n- A shape renamed in `startShape` alone would print a new key and leave the old key at zero; the same missing shared list is the root of both cases.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `startShape`'s comment states its order and its output vocabulary; `startState`'s JSDoc repeats the five names and the null case, so the public contract is documented even though the private consumer's declaration is not.\\n- `tallyBlock` copies `startShapes` rather than sharing the tally object, so a printed block cannot mutate the tally.\\n- The text summary prints all five shapes in a fixed insertion order, so a reader can compare two arms without parsing.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Raising the duplicated start rule (`startShape` versus `startedCommand`'s skill/report/expand/boundary sequence) as a finding: the two agree today, the comment in `readDocument` names both, and two instances do not justify a shared helper under the repository's restraint rule. Recorded as a follow-on risk, not a finding.\\n- Raising the missing shared shape-key constant twice (in `newTally` and in `startShape`'s literals): folded into the finding above as its fix rather than counted again.\\n- Calling the summary assertion `shapes.reduce(...) === 1` weak: its comment says it pins that the capped row adds no shape, and the same test's `startRate` assertion pins the started count, so it is fit for its stated purpose.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none; all four dimensions are covered and this is the third of three permitted iterations.\\n- Focus area: synthesis.\\n- Reason: `maxIterations` is reached; the remaining findings are three P2 advisories.\\n- Rotation status: swept.\\n- Required evidence: none outstanding.\\n- Run verdict for this lineage: PASS with advisories (3 active P2, 0 P1, 0 P0).\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-6/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816826031,"end":1794816839921}}}}
